WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.909
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.209 --> 00:00:08.677
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:15.960
Unit twenty-two: Festivals of Cambodia. Today you will describe Cambodian festivals using during and at.

4
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.947
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.319
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:24.917
Pchum Ben.

7
00:00:25.917 --> 00:00:29.484
Pchum Ben means a fifteen-day festival to honour ancestors.

8
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:32.431
During Pchum Ben, we bring food to the pagoda.

9
00:00:33.017 --> 00:00:35.414
Your turn. Say: Pchum Ben.

10
00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:39.291
Pchum Ben.

11
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.156
Khmer New Year.

12
00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.009
Khmer New Year means the Cambodian New Year in April.

13
00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:48.208
We play traditional games at Khmer New Year.

14
00:00:48.817 --> 00:00:51.306
Your turn. Say: Khmer New Year.

15
00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:55.725
Khmer New Year.

16
00:00:56.483 --> 00:00:57.775
Water Festival.

17
00:00:58.783 --> 00:01:02.373
Water Festival means a November festival with boat races.

18
00:01:02.983 --> 00:01:05.772
Millions visit Phnom Penh for the Water Festival.

19
00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:09.094
Your turn. Say: Water Festival.

20
00:01:11.933 --> 00:01:13.341
Water Festival.

21
00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:14.968
Pagoda.

22
00:01:15.983 --> 00:01:17.855
Pagoda means a Buddhist temple.

23
00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.053
My grandparents go to the pagoda every week.

24
00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:24.221
Your turn. Say: Pagoda.

25
00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:27.766
Pagoda.

26
00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:29.738
Ancestors.

27
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.992
Ancestors means family members who lived long ago.

28
00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:36.873
We remember our ancestors with prayers.

29
00:01:37.483 --> 00:01:39.973
Your turn. Say: Ancestors.

30
00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:43.892
Ancestors.

31
00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:45.698
Offering.

32
00:01:46.683 --> 00:01:49.658
Offering means a gift given to monks or spirits.

33
00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.366
We make an offering of rice and fruit.

34
00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:55.869
Your turn. Say: Offering.

35
00:01:58.733 --> 00:01:59.618
Offering.

36
00:02:00.383 --> 00:02:01.442
Boat race.

37
00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:06.075
Boat race means a competition between long, fast boats.

38
00:02:06.683 --> 00:02:08.938
Our village team won the boat race.

39
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:12.005
Your turn. Say: Boat race.

40
00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:16.042
Boat race.

41
00:02:16.783 --> 00:02:17.959
Celebrate.

42
00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:22.354
Celebrate means to do something enjoyable for a special day.

43
00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.321
We celebrate with music and dancing.

44
00:02:25.917 --> 00:02:28.941
Your turn. Say: Celebrate.

45
00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:32.848
Celebrate.

46
00:02:33.633 --> 00:02:37.261
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:38.117 --> 00:02:41.335
Visal, which Cambodian festival do you enjoy most?

48
00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.821
Khmer New Year! At Khmer New Year, we play traditional games.

49
00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:49.545
What do you do during Pchum Ben?

50
00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:55.610
During Pchum Ben, we visit the pagoda and make offerings for our ancestors.

51
00:02:56.717 --> 00:02:58.263
And the Water Festival?

52
00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:04.800
At the Water Festival, we watch the boat race by the river. It's so exciting!

53
00:03:05.967 --> 00:03:07.316
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:11.102
Grammar focus: During and at plus festival.

55
00:03:11.402 --> 00:03:12.646
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.814
During Pchum Ben, people visit pagodas.

57
00:03:16.717 --> 00:03:18.914
At Khmer New Year, we play games.

58
00:03:19.817 --> 00:03:23.093
During the Water Festival, crowds watch the boat race.

59
00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:28.439
'During' focuses on the whole time of the festival. 'At' means at that time of year.

60
00:03:29.183 --> 00:03:33.716
Be careful! Don't say: In Pchum Ben, people visit pagodas.

61
00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:38.897
Say: During Pchum Ben, people visit pagodas.

62
00:03:39.197 --> 00:03:41.208
Use 'during' or 'at' with festivals.

63
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.850
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:45.633 --> 00:03:46.901
Our Festivals.

65
00:03:47.201 --> 00:03:49.631
Cambodians celebrate many festivals.

66
00:03:50.633 --> 00:03:55.094
At Khmer New Year in April, families visit the pagoda and play games.

67
00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:59.365
During Pchum Ben, people make an offering for their ancestors.

68
00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:04.514
At the Water Festival, crowds watch the boat race on the river.

69
00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.870
These festivals connect our families and keep our culture strong.

70
00:04:09.967 --> 00:04:13.748
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:14.583 --> 00:04:17.175
blank Pchum Ben, people visit pagodas.

72
00:04:17.475 --> 00:04:20.432
A, During. B, In. C, On.

73
00:04:23.967 --> 00:04:25.502
The answer is A: During.

74
00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:28.522
A Buddhist temple is a blank.

75
00:04:28.822 --> 00:04:32.789
A, pagoda. B, boat race. C, offering.

76
00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:38.310
The answer is A: pagoda.

77
00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.181
Family members who lived long ago are our blank.

78
00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:46.483
A, ancestors. B, cousins. C, monks.

79
00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.184
The answer is A: ancestors.

80
00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.494
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.953
Which Cambodian festival do you enjoy most?

82
00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.297
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:10.597 --> 00:05:18.462
I enjoy the Water Festival most. During the festival, my family goes to the river to watch the boat races and see the fireworks.

84
00:05:18.762 --> 00:05:20.251
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:25.451
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and during and at plus festival.

86
00:05:25.751 --> 00:05:30.865
Today's value is cultural pride. Be proud of Khmer festivals and traditions.

87
00:05:31.165 --> 00:05:34.920
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

88
00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:37.849
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

